/**
  @page examples-mmg-simple_io Saving an MMG mesh
  @brief Write and reload geometry together with MMG feature metadata.

  @tableofcontents
  @m_footernavigation

  @section examples-mmg-io-intro Geometry and remeshing features

  `MMG::Mesh` extends the local geometry mesh with corner, ridge and required
  entity sets. These labels carry remeshing constraints in addition to the
  mesh's ordinary region and boundary attributes.

  @section examples-mmg-io-create Construct and mark the mesh

  The example scales an eight-by-eight vertex grid to the unit square and
  marks its four corners. Vertex zero is also marked as required.
  Boundary incidence is prepared before any facet queries.

  @snippet MMG/MeshIO.cpp mmg-io-create

  @section examples-mmg-io-save Save the metadata

  MEDIT represents MMG features through dedicated sections. Required vertices,
  edges, triangles and tetrahedra are written as their corresponding
  `RequiredVertices`, `RequiredEdges`, `RequiredTriangles` and
  `RequiredTetrahedra` sections when those sets are populated.

  @section examples-mmg-io-load Reload and compare

  The format argument selects the MEDIT reader explicitly. A second write
  makes the loaded representation available for inspection.

  @snippet MMG/MeshIO.cpp mmg-io-roundtrip

  The program compares mesh counts and the marked corner/required-vertex
  metadata. Preservation during a subsequent remeshing or level-set cut is
  covered separately by @ref examples-mmg-behavior.

  @section examples-mmg-io-full Build and run

  Build `MeshIO` and run it from a scratch directory. It writes
  `MMG.medit.mesh` and `MMG.copy.medit.mesh`; the expected mesh has 64 vertices
  and 98 triangles.

  The complete program is available in @ref MMG/MeshIO.cpp "MeshIO.cpp".

  @section examples-mmg-io-see-also Continue

  - @ref examples-mmg-casting "Mesh conversion and object lifetimes"
  - @ref examples-mmg-mesh_optimization "Optimize the geometry"
  - @ref guides-io "Other I/O formats"

  @example MMG/MeshIO.cpp
  @m_examplenavigation{examples-mmg-simple_io,MMG/}
  @m_footernavigation
*/
